Not swept, deliberately: bare ရုံး = "the firm" outside 012. The whole guidance pack (and the R1 link labels the
supervisor generated from it, e.g. "[ရုံးထံ မည်သို့ စာပေးပို့နိုင်သနည်း]" in 005/007/013/015) uses ရုံး as the
established Burmese term for the firm; changing it in 003/005/013/015 would desync the column link labels from
the pack titles. Only 012 was changed, where a litigation context makes ရုံး read as တရားရုံး (the court) — which
is the defect the reviewer actually described.

## Things I believe the reviewers got wrong (not applied)
1. my-a #1 — the suggested replacement gloss "(의료법)" is Hangul. The WO and the checker's `hangul` gate forbid
   Korean characters outside `url` values. Fixed by removing the gloss, not by swapping it.
2. my-a #7 / my-b #4 — "the English files have none [no U+200B]". True, but the checker's isomorphism baseline is
   the Korean source, which has exactly the same ZWSP count as the Burmese. Removing them is a hard FAIL on
   `blocks`, so this row cannot be closed inside the locale lane. Escalating rather than applying.
3. my-a #4, #5, my-b #23 — writing small cardinals and fractions as Burmese words is correct Burmese but the
   `numbers` check is a strict multiset comparison against the Korean source with zero headroom in all 18 files.
   The WO's own fallback ("prefer the form the checker accepts") applies.
4. my-a #3 — the reviewer judged the sentence against the EN ("were checked on 2026-07-25"); the Burmese was
   translated from the ko source, which says "…을 확인하는 출발점입니다" (is the starting point). I fixed the real
   defect ("1차 자료" mistranslated as "the 1st source", "official" dropped) and kept the ko framing rather than
   silently re-basing the sentence on the EN.
5. my-a #13 — "the amount is given twice and the second copy uses English shorthand M". The second copy is the
   token "TWD 1.57M" that a unit test pins byte-identical for all 45 locales (international-guidance-team.ts
   line 1858); vi/id/es/fr/pt/ar/ca/da all carry the same duplication. Only the word order was fixed.
6. my-b #18 also lists 017's "နောက်တစ်ခုတွင်" as the same fault — it is not a "former/latter" pair there, it refers
   back to the third of three listed thresholds, so ပထမ/ဒုတိယ would be wrong. Left as is.

